  "asked": "# Build: three-layouts-per-screen-r2 (ALL Opus, high thinking; this account has NO Fable) **Name:** Three layouts per screen · **Category:** Framework ## Resume (Brett, voice, Nov 5): restart the builds that died on credits, on Opus The first run (`/root/axf-builds/three-layouts-per-screen`) died at ~21:55 Nov 4 with 'out of usage credits'. **FIRST:** salvage its work: check its branch for pushed commits (`git -C /root/axf-builds/three-layouts-per-screen log --oneline origin/main..HEAD`) and its uncommitted changes (`git status --short` / `git diff`). Bring over ONLY the files that build actually wrote for this feature. **Never** copy builds-store/journal/orchestrator/report noise (`_claude/builds/*.json`, journals, other builds' reports). Continue from where it stopped; don't redo finished work. The full spec is that worktree's `.brief.md` (read it). In short: **new plugins only, not retrofitted**: every new plugin screen declares **3 layout variants** plus a **layout switcher toolbar hidden by default**; scaffolds generate them; CI enforces it for new plugins. The switcher references **one shared toolbar asset** (change once, changes everywhere) with right-click 'Give this plugin its own copy' / revert. Fit with what landed since: tab-group/chrome assets (#327), banner widgets (#352), and the Skins / Theme manager (Appearance) work if it has landed. **Brett's override:** do everything on Opus. Mark any new shared format 'Opus, possible Fable review' in the report + PR. Do NOT stop for Fable. Rules: resumable steps (progress file ticked + pushed after every step), book to a free named agent, tests, docs, UI Review shots (non-blocking). PR **through the merge queue only**. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
